UID:4bf013b921d2fc3a2dcfd2ed5c8e05d67465dc4e@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261004T001530Z
DTSTART:20261007T230000Z
DTEND:20261008T010000Z
SUMMARY:Queen Budapest
LOCATION:Kendall Square\, 355 Binney St\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:On July 27\, 1986\, Queen performed the largest-ever stadium co
 ncert at the Népstadion in Budapest in front of 80\,000 ecstatic fans. Th
 e concert was part of the famed Magic Tour\, which was the last time the b
 and toured with lead singer Freddie Mercury. Now\, this original concert f
 ilm has been beautifully rescanned and remastered in 4K alongside a dynami
 c new audio mix\, featuring many of Queen's favorite tracks — "Bohemian 
 Rhapsody\,” "Crazy Little Thing Called Love\," "I Want To Break Free” 
 and "We Are The Champions." With three years to go before the fall of the 
 Berlin Wall\, this was the first Western rock concert performed in a stadi
 um behind the then Iron Curtain. It was of such significance to the Hungar
 ian authorities and film industry that a group of the country’s top film
  cameramen and technicians were brought together to film it for posterity.
 \nhttps://booking.landmarktheatres.com/launch/ticketing/c095accd-a201-54fe
 -8c8d-db542c1ff71b\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://booking.landmarktheatres.com/launch/ticketing/c095accd-a201-54f
 e-8c8d-db542c1ff71b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2236b416e97ddf363c8ab02ddd15a201c51c5781@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261004T001530Z
DTSTART:20261007T231000Z
DTEND:20261008T011000Z
SUMMARY:Halloween (1978)
LOCATION:Kendall Square\, 355 Binney St\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:The film that redefined movie terror forever returns\, digitall
 y restored and remastered! On October 30\, 1978\, Michael Myers escapes a 
 sanitarium under the care of a psychiatrist (Donald Pleasence) and makes h
 is way back home\, turning a night of tricks and treats into something muc
 h more sinister for three young women—including Laurie Strode\, the star
 -making role for Jamie Lee Curtis. John Carpenter’s seminal 1978 classic
  premiered in cinemas and on drive-in screens over four decades ago\, chan
 ging the landscape of horror cinema.\nhttps://booking.landmarktheatres.com
 /launch/ticketing/607acab9-6d86-5c29-89fa-692e397b6427\nFrom Pushpin Bosto
 n: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://booking.landmarktheatres.com/launch/ticketing/607acab9-6d86-5c2
 9-89fa-692e397b6427
END:VEVENT
